e  president during impeachment proceedings  it could be done with all Democrats and  a few Republicans but that would be a  great situation for Republicans if  Democrats lead an impeachment  and then it fails on the conviction side  if if dot that happens Donald Trump is  completely re-energized and empowered  and I think that that's a really really  dangerous scenario now let's consider a  different scenario if Donald Trump is  convicted and impeached you have Trump a  give way to Mike Pence reliable for  religious conservatives helps the  Republican brand Republicans get the  benefits of impeachment with little risk  if just a few were to join Democrats and  that's another really risky scenario so  there's already a number of scenarios  here Pat where impeachment could  actually lead to Democrats being worse  off in both either or both 2018 and 2020  I do understand the concerns I just  think that if the allegations are true  and that the Trump campaign did collude  with Russia not only a foreign  government but an adversarial government  to help get him elected that that would  be so damning and the charges would be  tantamount to treason it would be to a  point where you kind of have to undergo  some impeachment proceedings you're  completely right and I am NOT arguing  that if the facts show that impeachment  is appropriate that impeachment should  not happen but sort of playing out how  these different scenarios might end up  impacting politics and Democrats for the  next two elections imagine another  scenario there is a democratic led  impeachment and it fails to impeach  Trump not only do you have Trump  re-energized as I mentioned you also are  probably helping Republicans in 2018 and  2020 as well and that could be really  dangerous when you think about what  would happen politically with continued  total Republican control in the House  and Senate and we can look at history  too because in 1998 of course  congressional Republicans led the charge  to impeach Bill Clinton and his approval  rating went up to 73 percent now I think  part of that has to do with the reason  that they tried to impeach Bill Clinton  over over sex scandal that's are more  important but you can see how it can  backfire so easily it could also  backfire a failed Democratic lead  impeachment could backfire because the  progressive movement right now is hugely  energized  do you realize what would happen to the  progressive movement that is so  energized right now if Democrats managed  to start impeachment proceedings with  the help of just a few Republicans and  those proceedings fail to remove Donald  Trump I don't know if you agree with me  Pat but that would hugely deflate the  momentum of the progressive movement  that is so energized right now I think  would also deflate the Trump agenda for  some time though they wouldn't be able  to really talk about health care and tax  reform if they're distracted by  impeachment proceedings and I think that  could help run out the clock to 2018 and  2020 the run out the clock idea I want  to get to in a second before I do that  though what if Republicans realize you  know what Trump is toxic we need to lead  impeachment that's better for Democrats  right because obviously Democrats would  support that impeachment if Republicans  are leading it there would be some  Republican voters who respect  Republicans saying hey you know what not  for the good of my party but for the  good of the country I as a Republican  will support the impeachment of Donald  Trump but you would have tons of  trumpets that would be mad at their  senators and members of Congress they  might not vote at all in 2018 or 2020 or  they might vote and vote Democratic to  punish those representatives that  they're angry with that's a better  scenario but it still might have the  potential to put Mike Pence in to  quietly destroy the country in far less  scandalous way or fashion than Donald  Trump so the best scenario and this sort 